  "notes": [
    "All modes retain 151 dense K4 projections, 78 fused RMS layers, and 78 attention lookup layers.",
    "MTP uses the production prefill input sizes and keeps batched target verification. Dense K4, residual/RMS, and attention lookup kernels support one to four token rows.",
    "The one- and three-draft-token MTP modes select the production kernels during target verification. Larger batches use the existing native paths.",
    "Previous MTP comparisons use the preceding suite. Fresh production controls report any speed drift; these are not interleaved old/new MTP pairs.",
    "All target verification row counts are compiled before timing, and an eight-output warmup runs before each timed request.",
    "First replies use the same cached 23861-token prompt. Follow-ups use the same production reply cache and 4469 new input tokens.",
    "Exactness is diagnostic. The user permits divergence when answer quality is close and measured speed gains are worthwhile.",
    "The exactness diagnostic compares tokens, text, all full log probability vectors, committed target cache values, and offsets.",
    "Allocated cache padding is diagnostic. Prefix preparation and fingerprint checks are outside timing."
  ]
